### =====================================================================
### Topic 5 School Portal (port 8085). Use the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
### REST Client turns "Basic user:password" into the proper Base64 header for you.
### =====================================================================

### 1. Public: no login needed -> 200
GET http://localhost:8085/public/notice-board

### 2. No login -> 401 Unauthorized (who are you?)
GET http://localhost:8085/me

### 3. Wrong password -> 401
GET http://localhost:8085/me
Authorization: Basic ada:wrongpassword

### 4. Logged in as ada -> 200
GET http://localhost:8085/me
Authorization: Basic ada:ada123

### 5. Student sees ONLY their own results
GET http://localhost:8085/results/my
Authorization: Basic ada:ada123

### 6. Student tries the admin area -> 403 Forbidden (we know you, but no)
GET http://localhost:8085/admin/users
Authorization: Basic ada:ada123

### 7. Admin opens the admin area -> 200
GET http://localhost:8085/admin/users
Authorization: Basic admin:admin123

### 8. Teacher records a score -> 201
POST http://localhost:8085/results
Authorization: Basic mrbello:teach123
Content-Type: application/json

{ "student": "tunde", "subject": "Physics", "score": 81 }

### 9. Student tries to record a score -> 403
POST http://localhost:8085/results
Authorization: Basic ada:ada123
Content-Type: application/json

{ "student": "ada", "subject": "Maths", "score": 100 }

### 10. Tunde checks his results (should include Physics now)
GET http://localhost:8085/results/my
Authorization: Basic tunde:tunde123

### 11. Admin clears all results -> 204
DELETE http://localhost:8085/admin/results
Authorization: Basic admin:admin123
